// Pseudo-code for event dispatcher
while (true) {
  for (room of roundRobinSchedule()) {
    if (room.buffer.hasEvents() && globalQueue.notFull()) {
      globalQueue.enqueue(room.buffer.dequeue());
    } else if (globalQueue.isFull()) {
      applyBackpressure();
    }
  }
}
```

## Test Plan
1. **Per-room ordering**: Send concurrent events to same room, verify FIFO processing
2. **Degradation behavior**: Flood system to trigger threshold, verify non-critical events are dropped/debounced
3. **Graceful shutdown**: Stop accepting new events, process remaining queue, verify no data loss

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of multi-stage concurrency, per-key ordering across stages, and robust backpressure propagation. Requires designing data structures that preserve ordering while allowing parallelism and handling dynamic worker changes.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-stage bounded pipelines with per-key sequencing
- Cross-stage backpressure and credit-based flow control
- Late/out-of-order handling with per-key versioning
- Dynamic worker resizing and fairness under load

## Code Example

```javascript
class PerKeySequencer {
  constructor() {
    this.map = new Map();
  }
  next(key, seq) {
    const prev = this.map.get(key) || Promise.resolve();
    const nextP = prev.then(() => seq);
    this.map.set(key, nextP);
    return nextP;
  }
}
```

